Package: deconflate
Type: Package
Title: Comorbidity Adjustment of Disease Impact Estimates
Version: 0.3.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Philip", "Rasmussen", email = "phr@sund.ku.dk",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Adjusts ("de-conflates") single-disease impact estimates for
    statistical associations between diseases, so that impacts can be
    aggregated without double counting. Implements an exact simultaneous
    solution of the additive impact equations of Rasmussen et al. (2022)
    <doi:10.1016/j.prevetmed.2022.105617> for crude estimates and for
    coefficients of additive regressions with recorded adjustment sets
    (the published proportional approximation is kept for comparison and
    reproduction), and a global model that fits a maximum-entropy
    distribution of disease combinations by iterative proportional fitting,
    fills in pairs without an association estimate, and incorporates
    specified pairwise impact interactions and three-way association
    scenarios. Event impacts (hazard ratios, rate ratios, risk ratios, odds
    ratios and risk differences of, e.g., culling) are adjusted with a
    snapshot hazard model, with the risk attributable to disease. Includes
    Shapley attribution, feasibility checks, propagation of input
    uncertainty with stability diagnostics, threshold searches, sensitivity
    screening and reproduction of the published analyses.
